       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day for adults. Higher doses mostly add peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, with little extra blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** I'll enter it if you confirm the dose is intentional. I can add a note such as \"Dose above usual max, confirmed with attending.\"\n3. **A different regimen.** If the goal is more blood pressure control, you could add a second agent instead, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic."
